# code-repo-scope-check.yml.template — kit-shipped CI recipe for a NESTED CODE REPOSITORY
# (kit feature 012, GAP-016; docs/sdlc/repository-strategy.md, "Territory across
# repositories"). Its sibling, project-gate.yml.template, runs your gate; this one runs
# Definition of Done gate 4 — the machine scope check — over this repository's phase
# commits.
#
# WHY IT EXISTS: in the nested layout the Territory declaration lives in the GOVERNANCE
# repository (specs/NNN-name/tasks.md) while the code lives here. Governance CI clones the
# governance repository alone and reports `n/a` for this repository; this workflow closes
# that gap from the other side by checking out the governance repository as a sibling and
# running its checker against this repository's commits.
#
# The `.template` suffix keeps this file inert — GitHub never runs it. To use it:
#
#   1. COPY it into THIS CODE REPOSITORY as .github/workflows/code-repo-scope-check.yml.
#      Leave the template untouched in the governance repository: it is surgical-class, so
#      kit updates report upstream changes but never rewrite your filled copy.
#   2. Fill GOVERNANCE_REPO with `owner/name` of the governance repository, and
#      CODE_REPO_DIR with this repository's directory name EXACTLY as it is declared in
#      the governance repository's kit-adoption.json `codeRepos` — the check prefixes this
#      repository's paths with that name before matching territory entries. A name that is
#      not in `codeRepos` fails the job with an error naming the declared set.
#   3. Private governance repository: create a read-only token (a fine-grained PAT with
#      Contents: read, or a GitHub App token) and store it as the GOVERNANCE_TOKEN secret.
#      Public governance repository: delete the `token:` line. NEVER inline a credential.
#   4. Feature branches must share the same NNN-name in both repositories (the
#      Cross-Repository Feature Rule) — that is what lets the check find the declaration.
#      The governance checkout below uses the SAME ref name for exactly this reason; the
#      checker also falls back to the remote-tracking ref, so a governance branch that was
#      never checked out locally still resolves.
#
# READING A RUN: PASS or FAIL means the check graded this repository. A run that reports
# only WARN or n/a graded NOTHING — the wiring is wrong (a mismatched CODE_REPO_DIR, a
# governance branch that does not exist, or a code repository whose trunk is not main:
# pass -BaseRef). Do not treat that as a green gate.
#
# What a run means: PASS/not applicable/WARN exit 0; FAIL (an undeclared path) exits 1 and
# names the file. A repository with no matching branch, or a phase with no declaration yet,
# is reported and does not fail the run. Recommended once it has run: require the
# `code-repo-scope-check` status check on this repository's main
# (docs/sdlc/branch-protection.md).

name: code-repo-scope-check

# PUSH EVENTS ONLY, deliberately: actions/checkout gives a real local branch on a push,
# while a pull_request checkout is a detached merge preview with no NNN-name branch — the
# checker would report 'no branch here' and pass without grading anything. The push-event
# run is also the one CI-held certification cites (docs/sdlc/gate-command.md).
on:
  push:
    branches:
      - '[0-9][0-9][0-9]-*'

permissions:
  contents: read

jobs:
  code-repo-scope-check:
    runs-on: ubuntu-latest
    steps:
      - name: Check out this code repository
        uses: actions/checkout@v4
        with:
          # the checker walks this branch's history back to its merge base with main
          fetch-depth: 0
          path: '{{CODE_REPO_DIR}}'

      - name: Check out the governance repository as the parent
        uses: actions/checkout@v4
        with:
          repository: '{{GOVERNANCE_REPO}}'
          # the feature's declaration lives on the matching governance branch, not on main
          ref: ${{ github.ref_name }}
          # delete this line when the governance repository is public
          token: ${{ secrets.GOVERNANCE_TOKEN }}
          # the declaration is read as of each code commit's date — full history required
          fetch-depth: 0
          # nothing after checkout needs the credential; the checker never fetches
          persist-credentials: false
          path: governance

      - name: Nest the code repository inside the governance checkout
        shell: bash
        env:
          CODE_REPO_DIR: '{{CODE_REPO_DIR}}'
        run: mv "$CODE_REPO_DIR" "governance/$CODE_REPO_DIR"

      - name: Machine scope check against the declared territory
        shell: pwsh
        working-directory: governance
        # The branch name goes through an env var, NEVER interpolated into `run:` —
        # github.head_ref is attacker-controlled on fork PRs and refnames may contain
        # shell metacharacters (same hardening as ritual-checks.yml).
        env:
          SCOPE_BRANCH: ${{ github.ref_name }}
          CODE_REPO_DIR: '{{CODE_REPO_DIR}}'
        run: >
          ./scripts/scope-check-repos.ps1
          -Repo $env:CODE_REPO_DIR
          -Branch $env:SCOPE_BRANCH
          -All
